      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:173:5",
      "text": [
        " رَمَى أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) الْجَمْرَةَ الْعُظْمَى فَرَأَى النَّاسَ وُقُوفاً فَقَامَ وَسْطَهُمْ ثُمَّ نَادَى بِأَعْلَى صَوْتِهِ أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إِنَّ هَذَا لَيْسَ بِمَوْقِفٍ ثَلَاثَ مَرَّاتٍ فَفَعَلْتُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad,f rom Muhammad Bin Sinan, from Ibn Muskan, from Saeed Al Roumy who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> pelted <span class=\"iTxt\">Al-Jamarah </span>Al-Uzmah (the bigger <span class=\"iTxt\">Jamarah</span>), so he<sup>asws</sup> saw the people having paused. So he<sup>asws</sup> stood up in their midst, then called out in a loud voice of his<sup>asws</sup>: ‘O you people! This is not a Pausing Stop!’ – three times. So I did it (as well)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. A number of our people have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn Sinan from ibn Muskan from Sa‘id al- Rumiy who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, threw pebbles on al-Jamarah al-‘Uzma’ and saw people standing. He (the Imam) stood in their middle and announced with the height of his voice, ‘O people, this is not a station’, three times, and I did it (as he (the Imam) had done).” "
        ]
      }
    },
